{"book":"congruence","bookTitle":"Congruence and similarity","concept":7,"title":"Finding sides in similar triangles","grades":"Grade 9","goal":"I can calculate unknown sides in similar triangles.","teach":"Find the scale factor from one pair of matching sides, then multiply (or divide). Or write equal ratios: if ΔABC ||| ΔDEF then <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\"><i>AB</i></span><span class=\"d\"><i>DE</i></span></span> = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\"><i>BC</i></span><span class=\"d\"><i>EF</i></span></span> = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\"><i>AC</i></span><span class=\"d\"><i>DF</i></span></span>. With DE ∥ BC in ΔABC, use <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\"><i>AD</i></span><span class=\"d\"><i>AB</i></span></span> = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\"><i>DE</i></span><span class=\"d\"><i>BC</i></span></span> (whole sides, not parts).","tvis":"<div class=\"vis\"><span class=\"vi\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:395px;height:auto\" viewBox=\"0 0 304 224\"><g transform=\"translate(22.0,24.0)\"><line x1=\"120.0\" y1=\"10.0\" x2=\"10.0\" y2=\"170.0\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"10.0\" y1=\"170.0\" x2=\"250.0\" y2=\"170.0\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"250.0\" y1=\"170.0\" x2=\"120.0\" y2=\"10.0\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"76.0\" y1=\"74.0\" x2=\"172.0\" y2=\"74.0\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><path d=\"M118.0,79.0 L124.0,74.0 L118.0,69.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><path d=\"M124.0,175.0 L130.0,170.0 L124.0,165.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><text x=\"120.0\" y=\"3.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">A</text><text x=\"0.0\" y=\"183.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">B</text><text x=\"260.0\" y=\"183.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">C</text><text x=\"64.0\" y=\"79.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">D</text><text x=\"184.0\" y=\"79.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">E</text><text x=\"55.0\" y=\"40.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">3</text><text x=\"25.0\" y=\"125.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">6</text><text x=\"124.0\" y=\"68.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">4</text><text x=\"130.0\" y=\"188.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">BC = ?</text></g></svg></span></div>","ex":{"q":"DE ∥ BC, AD = 3, DB = 6 and DE = 4. Find BC.","steps":["AB = 3 + 6 = 9, so the scale factor is 9 ÷ 3 = 3.","BC matches DE.","BC = 4 × 3 = 12."]},"watch":"Use the whole side AB = AD + DB, not DB on its own.<br><br><b>Problem-solving lens</b><br>Pull the small triangle out and draw it separately, the same way round as the big one.","qs":[{"text":"ΔABC ||| ΔDEF, AB = 5, DE = 15 and DF = 12. Find AC.","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"AC","a":"4","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"12 ÷ 3","steps":"1. Formula: scale factor k = new length ÷ old length (or big ÷ small for matching sides)<br>2. k = DE ÷ AB = 15 ÷ 5 = 3<br>3. AC = DF ÷ k = 12 ÷ 3 = 4"},{"text":"ΔPQR ||| ΔXYZ, PQ = 4, XY = 10 and QR = 6. Find YZ.","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"YZ","a":"15","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"6 × 2,5","steps":"1. Formula: scale factor k = new length ÷ old length (or big ÷ small for matching sides)<br>2. k = 10 ÷ 4 = 2,5<br>3. YZ = 6 × 2,5 = 15"},{"text":"The scale factor is 2,5. A side of the small triangle is 8 cm. Find the matching side of the big one.","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"Length (cm)","a":"20","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"8 × 2,5","steps":"1. Formula: scale factor k = new length ÷ old length (or big ÷ small for matching sides)<br>2. big side = 8 cm × 2,5<br>3. = 20 cm"}]}